  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wildlife Without Borders-Western Hemisphere</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;In contrast with its high degree of marginalization and poverty, the Ejido of Tumbisca features multiple ecosystems each with a high level of biodiversity and endemism. ENES is working with the community to secure the long term conservation of their natural resources and to promote their socio-economic wellbeing. Through this grant, the Recipient will: 1) deliver workshops on community governance, participation, decision making, and zoning; 2) organize exchange visits to neighboring communities that are successfully managing their natural resources; 3) implement workshops on sustainable forest management and ecoagricultural techniques; and 4) plan and implement a training program for 12 environmental community promoters..&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
